# Cloudflare Pages redirects & rewrites (Netlify-style, native to Pages).
# Astro builds with format:"file", so every page is a flat *.html file.

# Pages natively auto-serves an HTML asset when the extension is omitted
# (e.g. /about -> about.html) and 308-redirects *.html back to the clean URL.
# Adding our own 200-rewrite rules here caused a redirect loop, so the
# extensionless internal links (/about, /how-to-use, /roman-to-unicode,
# /contact, /advertise) rely on that built-in clean-URL behaviour instead.

# Old landing-page aliases -> permanent redirect to the home page.
/unicode-to-preeti      /        301
/unicode-to-preeti.html /        301

# The generated sitemap lives at /sitemap.xml; the intermediate
# sitemap-index.xml / sitemap-0.xml files are removed at build time, so keep
# them resolving for anything still pointing at the old URLs.
/sitemap-index.xml      /sitemap.xml 301
/sitemap-0.xml          /sitemap.xml 301

# Navigable error-page previews are served via clean URLs (HTTP 200); the real
# SEO-critical behaviour is native: any unmatched path falls back to the
# built-in 404.html and returns a genuine HTTP 404 status.
